{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Sub Drop",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: a deep sine bass that drops into each note from above, the punchy low end of big beat and breakbeat tracks (and a passable electronic kick on low notes).\n\nHow it's built: a sine two octaves down; a fast envelope into its FM bends the pitch down over the first few hundredths of a second; the amp envelope holds while the key is down; a little Drive adds harmonics so it's heard on small speakers.\n\nPlay: low notes, short and long.\n\nTweak: the pitch envelope's DECAY (longer is a slower drop, a 'boing'), the oscillator's FM (how far it drops), DRIVE.",
